re (injury / QB adjustments included).\n  3. Conference title games: top two in conference win %, ties broken by overall record then\n     (noisy) rating as a stand-in for real tiebreakers, played at a neutral site.\n  4. Committee proxy: r\u00e9sum\u00e9 score = simulated rating - 6 x losses + 3 for a conference title.\n     One loss is worth about a touchdown of rating, which tracks how committees have ranked.\n  5. 12-team field (2025+ format): the five highest-ranked conference champions plus the seven\n     best remaining, seeded straight by r\u00e9sum\u00e9; seeds 1-4 get byes, 5-8 host first-round games,\n     everything after is neutral.\nFCS opponents are a flat -22. All of this is a model of the committee, not the committee."}